# PART I — ENGLISH VERSION

## 1. Definitions

“VoxelCore” means the software project, its source code, binaries, documentation, associated files, updates, and official releases.

“Licensor” means the copyright holder of VoxelCore.

“User” means any individual or organization accessing, using, modifying, or distributing VoxelCore.

“Commercial Use” means using, incorporating, distributing, selling, licensing, or otherwise exploiting VoxelCore, directly or indirectly, for commercial advantage or monetary compensation.

“Net Profit” means the revenue attributable to commercial products or services that use, incorporate, or distribute VoxelCore, minus the permitted and documented direct expenses defined in Section 6.

## 2. Non-Commercial Permission

Subject to the terms of this License, the Licensor grants every User a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free permission to:

- Access and inspect the VoxelCore source code.
- Use VoxelCore for personal, educational, research, and other non-commercial purposes.
