## 3. Commercial Use Requires Permission

Commercial Use is **not permitted** under this License alone.

Any person or organization wishing to use VoxelCore commercially must first obtain explicit written permission from the Licensor and enter into a separate Commercial License Agreement.

Without that written permission, no User may:

- Sell VoxelCore or a product containing VoxelCore.
- Include VoxelCore in a paid product, service, modpack, or software package.
- Use VoxelCore to provide paid services.
- Monetize a product or service through its use of VoxelCore.
- Distribute VoxelCore as part of a commercial offering.

The Licensor may approve or reject commercial license requests.

## 4. Commercial Royalty

Unless a separate written agreement expressly provides otherwise, an approved commercial licensee must pay the Licensor **10% of the Net Profit** attributable to the commercial use of VoxelCore.

This royalty applies only to commercial activities covered by the relevant Commercial License Agreement.

The separate agreement must identify the licensed products, permitted activities, reporting requirements, payment schedule, and any agreed exceptions.

## 5. Ownership and Intellectual Property

VoxelCore and its original components remain the intellectual property of the Licensor and their respective contributors.

This License does not transfer ownership of VoxelCore to any User or commercial licensee.

Users retain ownership of their independently created contributions, subject to any separate agreements and applicable third-party rights.

No rights to the VoxelCore name, logo, or trademarks are granted by this License. Any commercial use of those marks requires separate written permission.

## 6. Net Profit Calculation

For the purpose of calculating the 10% royalty:

**Net Profit = Attributable Revenue − Permitted Direct Expenses**

“Attributable Revenue” means revenue reasonably attributable to products or services that use, incorporate, or distribute VoxelCore.

If VoxelCore is included in a larger product, revenue must be allocated using a reasonable, consistent, and documented method reflecting VoxelCore's contribution to that product.

“Permitted Direct Expenses” means reasonable, necessary, directly attributable, and documented costs of producing, distributing, and selling the relevant commercial product or service.

General company overhead, unrelated business expenses, artificial or inflated expenses, and costs not directly attributable to the licensed commercial activity may not be deducted.

Sales taxes, VAT, and similar transaction taxes collected on behalf of authorities are excluded from revenue. Income taxes are not deductible unless the separate Commercial License Agreement expressly allows them.

The licensee must maintain accurate financial records supporting its calculations.

## 7. Reporting, Payment, and Audit

Unless otherwise agreed in writing:

- Royalty calculations must be prepared quarterly.
- The licensee must submit a report within 30 days after the end of each calendar quarter.
- The 10% royalty must be paid within the same 30-day period.
- Reports must include attributable revenue, permitted expenses, Net Profit, and the royalty due.

The Licensor may, upon reasonable prior notice and no more than once per calendar year, request access to relevant records to verify royalty calculations.

If an audit identifies an underpayment of more than 5% for the audited period, the licensee must pay the shortfall and reasonable audit costs.

## 8. Termination

Permission under this License terminates automatically if a User materially violates its terms.

Where the violation can be corrected, the User will have 30 days after receiving written notice to correct it.

Upon termination, the User must stop the activities that are no longer authorized and stop distributing the affected copies.

Termination does not remove payment obligations or other liabilities that arose before termination.

